<H3><a name="I18n">Internationalisation support</a></H3>

<p>We can give you the right advice on the choices available to you once you decide to make your software or website international.  Before you even start the internationalisation process you have a number of decisions to make. We can help you </p>
<ul>
	<li>Deciding what languages and locales you need</li>
	<li>Deciding your localisation approach</li>
	<li>Identifying what needs localisation</li>
	<li>Deciding broad test conditions &#8211; operating systems/browsers, etc.</li>
	<li>Integrating the right localisation workflow, using the right technology, into your development environment</li>
</ul>
<p>Once you've defined the scale and scope of your task, you can begin estimating the effort your internationalisation process will need. Among the things you'll need to consider are listed below. We can provide you with the tools you need to cover each of these points efficiently and effectively.</p>
<ul>
	<li>Getting your source language right</li>
	<li>Creating an inventory of your localizables</li>
	<li>Making your code localisation-friendly</li>
	<li>Checking whether you need scripts, etc.</li>
	<li>Drawing up your localisation workflow</li>
	<li>Deciding on formatting changes</li>
	<li>Leveraging internationalisation features in your software architecture</li>
	<li>Using dummy translations to test run the workflow</li>
</ul>
